================================================================================
## Explorer Job actions: verify the run, show it in a popup, follow it in Background Tasks
================================================================================

Context:
Triggering a class Job from Explorer gave no popup and no confirmation that
the run had actually started: a toast appeared only after `run_now`
returned, and Background Tasks showed a generic message. The user asked for
a popup that verifies the job is running, informs the user immediately, and
follows the run state through Background Tasks.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/jobs/JobActionRunner.py
   New `run_state(run_id)`: one `get_run` returning `life_cycle_state`,
   `result_state`, `message` and `run_page_url`; SDK errors become
   InfrastructureError.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/node/JobActionService.py
   After `run_now`, the run state is read once (`_verified_state`, never fails
   the trigger; falls back to UNKNOWN). The response carries `run_state`,
   `run_page_url` and a message naming the state ("Job X is running" /
   "is queued" / "was started"). The Background Task starts with
   "Databricks run N: Running", stores `life_cycle_state` and `run_page_url`
   in its result, and each poll updates both (`_record_progress`).
3. src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py
   `NodeActionResponse.run_state` added.
4. src/front/static/query/js/query-dashboard.js
   - Shared `_showEntityActionModal` / `_actionSpinner` (UC functions and Jobs
     use the same modal; `bootstrap.Modal.getOrCreateInstance`).
   - Job actions open a popup immediately ("Starting job…"), then show the
     verified state with an icon and a label (Running / Queued / Starting),
     the run id, an "Open run in Databricks" link and a "Show Background
     Tasks" button; a success notification fires at once.
   - While the popup is open it polls `/tasks/<task_id>` every 3 s and moves
     to Succeeded / Failed / Cancelled; closing the popup stops polling.
   - `_jobRunStatus` maps task status + life-cycle state to icon/label.
   - Job branch removed from `_runEntityAction` (UC functions only).
5. src/front/static/global/js/task-tracker.js
   Background Task items show "Open run in Databricks" when the task result
   has an http(s) `run_page_url` (escaped, `rel="noopener"`).
6. Docs: docs/api.md (`run_state`, verified message), docs/user-guide.md
   (Job popup and Background Tasks), releases/ReleaseNotes_V0.9.0.md.
7. Tests
   - tests/units/core/test_job_action_runner.py: `run_state` read once, SDK
     error wrapped.
   - tests/units/dtwin/test_job_action_service.py: running / queued /
     state-check-failure responses, live state recorded on the task.
   - tests/units/api/test_node_job_action.py: `run_state` and `run_page_url`
     in the API response.
   - tests/units/front/test_class_actions_ui.py: Job popup contract, Node
     check of the status mapping (icon + label for every state), run link in
     Background Tasks.

